namespace NativeLogical

abbrev Mask := JuliaLean.base.multidimensional.Models1Group6.NativeLogical.Mask
abbrev ElementType := JuliaLean.base.multidimensional.Models1Group6.NativeLogical.ElementType
abbrev Value := JuliaLean.base.multidimensional.Models1Group6.NativeLogical.Value

/-- Necessary representation invariants of the initialized native Array{Bool}
storage projection. A Julia type's dimension tuple has machine arity; native
Bool storage has nonnegative length strictly below typemax(Int), the runtime
GenericMemory address-width limit (ordinary allocation is stricter by one,
while unsafe_wrap uses this limit). Rank-zero arrays have exactly one element.

The input is already an initialized array snapshot. This condition is not an
allocator-success promise or a claim that arbitrary handle/storage pairs
construct a native array. It permits every initialized storage projection in
this declared native scope, including empty positive-rank arrays. The bound
ensures the supplied word/tail count loops' Nat indices agree with their Julia
Int counterparts without imposing a separate arithmetic no-overflow premise.
Source: base/boot.jl:82-85,812-833; base/essentials.jl:12-13,1296;
